/*Q12. The Galactic Explorers Guild is preparing for a new expedition and wants to analyze the experience levels of its crew members. Design a
Java class named CrewMember to represent individual crew members and calculate their average experience level.
Class: CrewMember
The CrewMember class should contain the following attributes:
• name (String): Represents the name of the crew member.
• experienceLevel (int): Represents the experience level of the crew member.
Implement a parameterized constructor:
• CrewMember(String name, int experienceLevel) — initializes the crew member with the given name and experience level.
Maintain the information about all crew members using the following private static variables:
• crewMembers (CrewMember[]) — stores the objects representing all crew members.
• totalCrewMembers (int) — tracks the total number of crew members created.
Implement a static method named calculateAverageExperience() that calculates the sum of all crew members' experience levels, computes
their average using floating-point division, and displays the result rounded to two decimal places.
The CrewMember class must perform the following operations:
1. Read the number of crew members.
2. Create an array to store the crew member objects.
3. Read each crew member's name and experience level.
4. Create a CrewMember object for each crew member and store it in the array.
5. Invoke calculateAverageExperience() after all crew members have been created.
Input Format:
• The first line contains an integer representing the number of crew members.
• For each crew member, the following two values are provided in order:
<name>
<experience_level>
• This input is repeated for all crew members.
Output Format:
• Display the average experience level in the following format:
Average experience level: <average _experience_level>
• The average experience level must be rounded to two decimal places.
*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
public class CrewMember {
    String name;
    int experienceLevel;
 
    private static CrewMember[] crewMembers;
    private static int totalCrewMembers = 0;
 
    CrewMember(String name, int experienceLevel) {
        this.name = name;
        this.experienceLevel = experienceLevel;
        totalCrewMembers++;
    }
 
    static void calculateAverageExperience() {
        int sum = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < totalCrewMembers; i++) {
            sum += crewMembers[i].experienceLevel;
        }
        double avg = totalCrewMembers == 0 ? 0.0 : (double) sum / totalCrewMembers;
        System.out.printf("Average experience level: %.2f%n", avg);
    }
 
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int n = Integer.parseInt(sc.nextLine().trim());
        crewMembers = new CrewMember[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            String name = sc.nextLine().trim();
            int level = Integer.parseInt(sc.nextLine().trim());
            crewMembers[i] = new CrewMember(name, level);
        }
        calculateAverageExperience();
        sc.close();
    }
}
